rules matching merchant profile + each transaction? Let's compute union of rule IDs matching each transaction on day 10 under monthly metrics of January. Need include all card schemes present, is_credit, aci, intracountry. Could be many but manageable. Need understand \"For the 10th of the year 2023\" maybe they want fees applicable to that day's transactions. Day 10 is January 10. Monthly metrics based on January full month? Manual: monthly fraud/volume computed natural months starting day1 ending last day. For a transaction on Jan 10, the monthly value should be based on whole January (ex post) perhaps. Since dataset has full month data. Likely yes.\n\nBut could be \"for the 10th\" means compute monthly metrics from January 1-10 (data available up to that date)? Manual says monthly volumes/rates computed natural months fully. So full month.\n\nLet's compute union for day 10 transactions using Jan monthly metrics. Also Q1753 March union. Need define match exactly:\n- card_scheme exact to transaction's scheme\n- account_type: merchant R in rule list or wildcard\n- capture_delay: merchant capture \"1\" maps <3, so rule capture null or \"<3\"\n- monthly_fraud_level: Jan rate 10.31 -> \">8.3%\" (or null)\n- monthly_volume: 113260 -> \"100k-1m\" (or null)\n- merchant_category_code: merchant 5942 in list or wildcard\n- is_credit: rule is None or equal tx\n- aci: rule None/[] or tx in list\n- intracountry: rule None or equals (issuer country == acquirer country) => 1.0/0.0. Note acquirer_country per transaction.\n\nLet's compute candidate counts and unions."}
{"type": "tool_call", "callId": "call_00_psTMaNvsngesHrAVVV067273", "tool": "bash", "input": {"command": "cat > /tmp/analyze.py <<'PY'\nimport csv,json,collections,datetime,math\nfees=json.load(open('inputs/fees.json'))\nmd={m['merchant']:m for m in json.load(open('inputs/merchant_data.json'))}\n\ndef iswild(v): return v is None or v==[] \ndef field_match(rv,v):\n    if iswild(rv): return True\n    if isinstance(rv,list): return v in rv\n    return rv==v\n\ndef fraud_cat(rate):\n    # rate in percent\n    if rate < 7.2: return '<7.2%'\n    if rate <= 7.7: return '7.2%-7.7%'\n    if rate <= 8.3: return '7.7%-8.3%'\n    return '>8.3%'\n\ndef vol_cat(v):\n    if v < 100000: return '<100k'\n    if v <= 1000000: return '100k-1m'\n    if v <= 5000000: return '1m-5m'\n    return '>5m'\n\ndef cap_cat(c):\n    if c=='immediate': return 'immediate'\n    if c=='manual': return 'manual'\n    x=int(c)\n    if x<3: return '<3'\n    if x<=5: return '3-5'\n    return '>5'\n\n# load payments into list for convenience\npayments=[]\nwith open('inputs/payments.csv') as f:\n    for x in csv.DictReader(f):\n        x['day']=int(x['day_of_year']); x['month']=(datetime.date(2023,1,1)+datetime.timedelta(days=x['day']-1)).month\n        x['amount']=float(x['eur_amount']); x['credit']=x['is_credit']=='True'; x['fraud']=x['has_fraudulent_dispute']=='True'\n        x['dom']=1.0 if x['issuing_country']==x['acquirer_country'] else 0.0\n        payments.append(x)\n\ndef month_metrics(merchant,year,month):\n    sel=[x for x in payments if x['merchant']==merchant and int(x['year'])==year and x['month']==month]\n    vol=sum(x['amount'] for x in sel); fv=sum(x['amount'] for x in sel if x['fraud'])\n    return vol, fv, (100*fv/vol if vol else 0), sel\n\ndef matching_fees(tx, merchant, fc, vc):\n    m=md[merchant]\n    out=[]\n    for r in fees:\n        if r['card_scheme']!=tx['card_scheme']: continue\n        if not field_match(r['account_type'],m['account_type']): continue\n        if not field_match(r['capture_delay'],cap_cat(m['capture_delay'])): continue\n        if not field_match(r['monthly_fraud_level'],fc): continue\n        if not field_match(r['monthly_volume'],vc): continue\n        if not field_match(r['merchant_category_code'],m['merchant_category_code']): continue\n        if not field_match(r['is_credit'],tx['credit']): continue\n        if not field_match(r['aci'],tx['aci']): continue\n        if not field_match(r['intracountry'],tx['dom']): continue\n        out.append(r)\n    return out\n\nif __name__=='__main__':\n    merchant='Belles_cookbook_store'\n    for mon in [1,3]:\n        vol,fv,rate,sel=month_metrics(merchant,2023,mon)\n        fc=fraud_cat(rate); vc=vol_cat(vol)\n        print('MONTH',mon,'vol',vol,'rate',rate,'fc',fc,'vc',vc,'n tx',len(sel))\n        ids=collections.Counter()\n        for tx in sel:\n            for r in matching_fees(tx,merchant,fc,vc): ids[r['ID']]+=1\n        print('all month union',len(ids),sorted(ids))\n        dsel=[x for x in sel if x['day']==10]\n        ids10=collections.Counter()\n        for tx in dsel:\n            for r in matching_fees(tx,merchant,fc,vc): ids10[r['ID']]+=1\n        print('day10 n tx',len(dsel),'union',len(ids10),sorted(ids10))\nPY\npython3 /tmp/analyze.py", "description": "Compute Belles fee unions for Jan/Mar"}}
